    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-25T09:36:35+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T09:36:35+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T23:06:35Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T23:06:35Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough and cold front continue moving across the far northeast on Sunday. A ridge of high pressure will move into the west late Sunday and persist over much of southern SA through to mid-next week, as the associated high slowly drifts east across waters to the south. A trough and low pressure system may then develop near the WA border from late Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW008" description="Mid North" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <warning-summary type="sheep_graziers_warning" start-time-local="2026-10-25T04:58:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T18:28:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">Warning to Sheep Graziers</warning-summary>
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers in the late morning and afternoon. Winds southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h tending south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the evening then becoming light in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 14 and 18.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of frost in the north in the early morning. Slight chance of a shower in the south in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Light winds becoming west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the middle of the day then becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 3 and 6 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the morning and afternoon. Light winds becoming south to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 6 with daytime temperatures reaching between 18 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of morning fog. Mostly sunny day. Light winds becoming southerly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon then tending southeasterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 6 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
